refs=sum(p['adequate'] for p in ps);lines+=['', f"Background references qualified in {refs}/{len(ps)} fresh paths. Every rejection remained in the unacquired denominator. Longer observation was evaluated only on these fixed emitted labels; no candidate, deadline or reference threshold was chosen after outcomes.",'', '## What the study supports', '', 'All 84 initially intact paths acquired with accurate first-confirmation geometry. Two-label confirmation had median observation 2 and range 1-15; three-label confirmation had median observation 3 and range 2-16. The third observation provided no demonstrated safety advantage here because both rules had zero observed false episodes. This is not proof that their risks are equal.', '', 'All 24 new births acquired: two-label latency was one or two observations after birth; three-label latency ranged from two to six. Acquisition timing matters independently of later retention: only 82/84 initially intact paths achieved the descriptive 90% post-acquisition single-label summary under either rule. Nothing in this result establishes uninterrupted particle persistence.', '', 'Zero false episodes in 60 initially invalid paths gives a pooled two-sided 95% upper probability limit of about 5.96%; zero in 32 early-damage paths gives about 10.9%. The per-defect bounds are wider. Thus this sample cannot establish a 5% bound for each control category, let alone a stronger general guarantee. No maximum latency or confirmation rule is chosen from these outcomes.', '', '## Correlation and information','', 'For a constant Gaussian mean with known AR1 correlation, a useful information reference is n_eff=1+(T-1)(1-rho)/(1+rho). At rho0.95, six observations provide about1.12821independent-observation equivalents and40provide2. This helps explain why observation count alone is a poor evidence budget. It is not a tracker-accuracy formula, does not cover changing geometry, and establishes no conversion of model time to seconds.','', '## Verification and retention','',f"Separate recomputation checked {c['labels']} frozen labels, {c['path_outcomes']} fresh path summaries for both confirmation lengths, {c['saved_development_checked']} saved-development records, {c['class_mode_mass_checks']} pair masses, {c['real_space_reference_quadratics']} real-space reference quadratics and {c['selected_history_quadratics']} history quadratics. Maximum selected quadratic difference was {c['max_selected_quadratic_difference']:.6g}. Driver explicit endpoint checks: {a['endpoint_checks']}. The checker used independent run-boundary/episode reconstruction, shared templates and the same author; this is not external replication.", '',f"Runtime: main {a['elapsed_seconds']:.6g}seconds; checker {c['elapsed_seconds']:.6g}seconds. Full fields, references and beam records remain in `local_raw/MG181_acquisition` ({raw['total_bytes']/1e6:.6g}MB), with a hash manifest. Public checkpoints retain calibration, model weights/guards, labels and metrics but omit beam arrays; these were compared exactly against the full local records.",'', '## Next decision and limits','','Prepare a prospective acquisition-state layer alongside the unchanged structural labels, with separate ACQUIRING, CONFIRMED and UNQUALIFIED states, no claim about pre-confirmation persistence, and explicit scene-change handling. Specify its false-acquisition and latency targets before a larger independent control test. Preserve the fixed structural instrument and confidence threshold while studying that policy. It does not choose or deploy a new rule, reclassify MG180 as passed, or establish calibrated optional-stopping probabilities. Any prospective acquisition policy needs an explicit safety/error target, sufficiently large independent invalid controls, treatment of scene changes during acquisition, and predictive/structural background-parameter uncertainty.','', 'Keep the structural instrument fixed while deciding that policy; do not simply pick the deadline that rescues the saved failures. The full method still assumes known spectral shape, supplied initial search anchor, externally available reference sets, finite template families and compressed histories. Physical particle persistence and G remain unresolved. MG180 and earlier verdicts are unchanged; no kinetic production or real-data rescore follows, and PI closure is pending.','', '![Cumulative valid acquisition](MG181_acquisition_curves.png)']
